      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The consensus among most mainstream economists suggests that unilateral protectionism is generally not a sustainable long-term strategy for a highly integrated global economy. Evidence often points to the in-\nefficiency and higher consumer costs that result from restricted global competition, which ultimately harms the very domestic sectors they are meant to support. Therefore, many view the success of these policies as more of a politically advantageous, short-term gain rather than a robust, enduring economic model.",
      "source": "target",
